        "answer": "You need good cardiovascular fitness and leg endurance. You should be able to comfortably walk 5 to 7 hours uphill on consecutive days carrying a 5 to 6 kg daypack. A dedicated 8- to 12-week training routine involving stair climbing, jogging, and weighted hill walks is strongly recommended."
