      {
        "question": "Which month in autumn is the single best for Annapurna Base Camp?",
        "answer": "October is widely considered the single best month. It offers the highest percentage of clear sunny days (averaging 27 sunny days), dry trails, stable avalanche conditions, and crystal-clear mountain visibility across Annapurna I, South, and Machapuchare."
      },
      {
        "question": "How cold does it get at Annapurna Base Camp in autumn?",
        "answer": "In October, daytime temperatures inside the sanctuary range from 10°C to 14°C in the sun, dropping to -5°C to -8°C at night inside unheated teahouse bedrooms. In November, nighttime temperatures drop to between -10°C and -12°C."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are there leeches on the ABC trail in autumn?",
        "answer": "No. By mid-October, the cool, dry air forces terrestrial leeches into dormant hibernation below the soil. You will not encounter active leeches on the trail during peak autumn."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do I need to book teahouses in advance for autumn?",
        "answer": "Yes! October and early November are the busiest trekking months in Nepal. Teahouses at Deurali and ABC operate at 100% capacity. Trekking with a registered agency like Igloo Himalaya Treks ensures your lodge beds are reserved in advance."
      },
      {
        "question": "What sleeping bag rating do I need for autumn?",
        "answer": "You need a down sleeping bag rated down to -10°C (14°F). While teahouses provide blankets, unheated bedrooms freeze at high altitude and an insulated sleeping bag is essential for warmth and hygiene."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I see festivals during an autumn trek?",
        "answer": "Yes! Nepal's two biggest religious festivals—Dashain (September/October) and Tihar (October/November)—take place during autumn. You will see decorated villages, bamboo swings, and evening singing celebrations along the trail."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is avalanche danger high in autumn?",
        "answer": "No. Autumn has the lowest avalanche danger of the year. The heavy summer monsoon melt has cleared old snow, and winter blizzards have not yet arrived, making the narrow Deurali to MBC corridor very safe."
      },
      {
        "question": "How many days do I need for the autumn ABC trek?",
        "answer": "A standard direct itinerary requires 7 to 9 days from Pokhara. If you wish to include the sunrise view from Poon Hill and visit Ghorepani, budget 10 to 13 days."
      }
