      {
        "id": "frequently-asked-questions",
        "h2": "5. Frequently Asked Questions",
        "content": "\n        <div class=\"faq-accordion\">\n          <details class=\"faq-item\">\n            <summary class=\"faq-question\">How easy is it to get a tourist visa on arrival in Nepal?</summary>\n            <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n              <p>Tourist visas are straightforward to obtain upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA) in Kathmandu for most nationalities. You can complete the electronic visa application at the automated kiosks in the arrival hall or pre-fill it online within 14 days of arrival via the Department of Immigration portal. Visa fees are payable in cash (USD, EUR, GBP) or by credit card: $30 for 15 days, $50 for 30 days, or $125 for 90 days.</p>\n            </div>\n          </details>\n          <details class=\"faq-item\">\n            <summary class=\"faq-question\">What is the tipping custom for guides and porters in Nepal?</summary>\n            <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n              <p>Tipping is customary and deeply appreciated in the tourism sector. For multi-day trekking expeditions, a standard guideline is approximately $15 to $20 USD per day for the trekking guide and $10 to $15 USD per day for porters, pooled among group members and presented on the final evening of the trek.</p>\n            </div>\n          </details>\n          <details class=\"faq-item\">\n            <summary class=\"faq-question\">Is it safe to travel in Nepal as a solo traveler?</summary>\n            <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n              <p>Nepal is widely recognized as one of the safest travel destinations in Asia for solo travelers, including solo female travelers. Violent crime is exceptionally rare. In mountain conservation areas, hiring a licensed guide ensures safety along remote paths and assists with lodge bookings and medical contingencies.</p>\n            </div>\n          </details>\n        </div>\n      "
      }
