    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Which is the single best month to trek Annapurna Base Camp?",
        "answer": "October is widely considered the single best month. It offers the highest percentage of clear sunny days (averaging 27 sunny days), dry trails, stable avalanche conditions, and crystal-clear mountain visibility across Annapurna I, South, and Machapuchare."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is spring or autumn better for Annapurna Base Camp?",
        "answer": "Both are fantastic. Autumn (October–November) offers clearer mountain views, dry trails, and lower avalanche risks. Spring (March–May) provides warmer daytime temperatures and blooming red and pink rhododendron forests, but has more afternoon clouds."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can you trek to Annapurna Base Camp in winter (December to February)?",
        "answer": "Yes! Winter trekking is possible for well-prepared hikers. While nighttime temperatures drop to between -12°C and -20°C at ABC, daytime skies are often crystal clear, trails are blissfully uncrowded, and teahouses are peaceful."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why should I avoid trekking during the monsoon (June to August)?",
        "answer": "The Pokhara basin receives the highest monsoon rainfall in Nepal. Trails are muddy, river canyons have high landslide risks, active leeches infest the bamboo forests below 3,000 meters, and mountain summits remain hidden behind thick clouds."
      },
      {
        "question": "When do the rhododendrons bloom along the ABC trail?",
        "answer": "The rhododendrons bloom from mid-March to late April, with the peak floral display occurring in the first two weeks of April between Ghorepani, Tadapani, Chhomrong, and Dovan."
      },
      {
        "question": "How cold does it get at Annapurna Base Camp in October?",
        "answer": "In October, daytime temperatures inside the sanctuary range from 10°C to 14°C in the sun, dropping to -5°C to -8°C at night inside unheated teahouse bedrooms."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is there an avalanche risk on the Annapurna Base Camp trail?",
        "answer": "Yes, the narrow corridor between Deurali (3,200 m) and Machapuchare Base Camp (3,700 m) has active avalanche paths. Risk is highest in late winter and early spring (February to April) when warming sunshine destabilizes heavy snowpacks."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do I need to book teahouses in advance for ABC?",
        "answer": "During the peak months of October, November, and April, teahouses at Deurali and ABC operate at 100% capacity. Trekking with a licensed agency like Igloo Himalaya Treks ensures your lodge beds are reserved ahead of time."
      }
    ],
