    "lead": "Setting off from the lakeside haven of Pokhara into the heart of the Annapurna Himalaya presents hikers with one of the most frequently asked dilemmas in modern trekking: Should you choose the legendary Annapurna Base Camp (ABC) trek, or the rapidly rising, knife-edge ridge of Mardi Himal? Both routes start within an hour's drive of Pokhara, fall under the protective boundary of the Annapurna Conservation Area Project (ACAP), and offer face-to-face encounters with sacred giants like Machapuchare, Annapurna South, and Hiunchuli. Yet their physical demands, visual perspectives, and daily atmospheres are entirely distinct. Annapurna Base Camp plunges you into a deep river canyon before delivering you into a 360-degree glaciated bowl beneath the 8,091-meter south face of Annapurna I—demanding that you conquer over 6,000 brutal stone stairs over 8 to 10 days. In contrast, Mardi Himal lifts you up onto a high mountain ridge in just 5 days, where you walk above the clouds on natural forest trails with constant eye-level panoramas. This definitive guide compares both treks across twelve crucial categories to help you select the ideal Himalayan adventure.",
