    "desc": "Comprehensive guide to annapurna base camp trek for beginners. Detailed itineraries, trail elevations, costs, avalanche zones, permit rules, and Sherpa pro-tips.",
    "lead": "If you have never set foot in the Himalaya—or if your hiking experience has been limited to weekend walks on gentle country trails—the prospect of trekking to Annapurna Base Camp (4,130m / 13,550ft) can feel both electrifying and deeply intimidating. Can a beginner with normal baseline fitness really hike to the foot of the world's 10th highest mountain? The short, definitive answer is an emphatic YES. Unlike grueling technical expeditions or 5,400-meter pass crossings, the Annapurna Sanctuary trek is supported every step of the way by established Gurung teahouse villages, freshly cooked hot meals, and well-trodden stone footpaths. However, being 'beginner-friendly' does not mean it is a walk in the park: you will climb over 6,000 unforgiving stone steps, hike 5 to 7 hours daily, sleep in unheated bedrooms, and enter thin high-altitude air where oxygen is 40% less dense than at sea level. This comprehensive first-timer's playbook walks you through every single step—from your 8-week stair-training blueprint and altitude acclimatization rules to gear selection, teahouse etiquette, and realistic daily budgets.",
    "readingTime": "21 min read",
