        "content": "\n        <p>\n          Successfully navigating travel and outdoor adventure in Nepal comes down to disciplined logistics. Follow these core field-tested principles:\n        </p>\n        <ol>\n          <li><strong>Plan Buffer Days:</strong> Mountain weather in the Himalayas is unpredictable. Always build at least two buffer days into your itinerary before international departures to account for highway delays or flight cancellations in Lukla or Pokhara.</li>\n          <li><strong>Filter All Drinking Water:</strong> Never drink unboiled tap water. Carry a reusable insulated water bottle paired with a SteriPEN UV purifier or chlorine dioxide purification tablets.</li>\n          <li><strong>Respect Sacred Spaces:</strong> When visiting Buddhist monasteries, Hindu shrines, or ancient palace squares, dress respectfully (shoulders and knees covered), ask permission before taking photos of monks or sadhus, and always walk clockwise around religious structures.</li>\n        </ol>\n      "
