    "quickAnswerTitle": "Quick Answer: What You Need to Know About Everest Base Camp Packing Mistakes to Avoid",
    "quickAnswerContent": "\n    <p><strong>Primary Trailhead & Flight:</strong> The journey begins with a flight from Kathmandu or Ramechhap to Lukla (2,846m), followed by a gradual 65km (one-way) trek up the Dudh Koshi valley to Everest Base Camp (5,364m) and Kala Patthar (5,545m).</p>\n    <p><strong>Key Requirements:</strong> Minimum 12 to 14 days required for safe acclimatization (with mandatory two-night rest stops in Namche Bazaar at 3,440m and Dingboche at 4,410m). Sagarmatha National Park Permit (NPR 3,000) and Khumbu Pasang Lhamu Municipality Entry Permit (NPR 3,000) are required.</p>\n    <p><strong>Best Travel Windows:</strong> Spring (March to May) for rhododendron blooms and Everest climbing expedition activity; Autumn (late September to November) for crystal-clear Himalayan visibility and stable mountain weather.</p>\n    <p><strong>Safety Golden Rule:</strong> Never ascend more than 300–500m sleeping elevation per day above 3,000m, drink 4 liters of purified water daily, and never ignore symptoms of Acute Mountain Sickness (AMS).</p>\n  ",
