    "lead": "While Annapurna Base Camp and Poon Hill draw thousands of trekkers each season, a quieter, wilder alternative runs along a high grassy spine just a few ridgelines away: the Khopra Ridge Trek, also known as Khopra Danda. Rising above Ghorepani and Tadapani to a rugged crest at 3,660 metres, Khopra offers uninterrupted views of Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Dhaulagiri, and Nilgiri, with the option of an extension to the sacred alpine Khayer Lake at 4,660 metres. The route is supported by community-run lodges that fund local schools and clinics, giving it an authentic, low-impact character that many popular trails have lost. This guide covers everything you need to plan Khopra: the geography, day-by-day itineraries, the Khayer Lake extension, difficulty, lodge conditions, permits, costs, and seasonal advice.",
